      <div class="what-we-do-text" data-aos="fade-left">
        <h3 class="legacy-sub-heading" data-i18n="roots_heading">From Ancient Roots to New Horizons</h3>
        
        <p data-i18n="roots_paragraph">
          Tharlam Monastery, a revered Sakya Buddhist institution whose full name is <strong>Shree Tharlam Sasang Namgyal Ling Monastery</strong>, traces its origins to <strong>1436</strong>. It was originally established by <strong>Ga Rabjampa Kunga Yeshe</strong> in <strong>Kham, Eastern Tibet</strong>, beginning its long and significant journey as a center for Buddhist teachings and practice.
        </p>
        
        <p data-i18n="legacy_reestablishment_details">
            Centuries later, its legacy was faithfully rebuilt. In <strong>1981</strong>, the monastery was re-established in <strong>Boudhanath, Kathmandu, Nepal</strong>, by <strong>Dezhung Rinpoche</strong>. This profound re-establishment fulfilled the specific instructions of his guru, <strong>Gaton Dorjechang</strong>, ensuring the spiritual and material continuity of Tharlam Monastery's enduring tradition for future generations.
        </p>
        
      </div>
    </div>
    
    <hr class="section-divider">

    <div class="what-we-do-grid content-grid-reversed"> 
